WEBVTT

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.680
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.800
(NEMO SCREAMS)

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.520
-Nemo!
-Nemo!

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:13.480
Dad!

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.680
-Nemo!
-Dad!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.920
No!

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.400
Nemo, hold on to me and don't let go!

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.080
Dad!

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.400
No, no! No!

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.520
(MARLIN GRUNTS)

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.680
(DORY PANTING)

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.400
Dory! Dory, slow down!
We're not being chased anymore.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.440
Are you sure? (SCREAMS)

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.960
(DORY GRUNTS)

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.600
Jenny and Charlie. Jenny and Charlie!

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.280
I just remembered their names!
We have to keep going. We're so close.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.560
-Huh?
-Nemo, are you hurt?

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.280
(GASPS) Oh my goodness! Nemo!
Are you okay? What happened?

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.120
-Not now, Dory. Please!
-Oh no.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.600
-Nemo. Oh no. Oh no.
-I'm okay.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.760
Oh, Nemo. I'm sorry. Okay. I'm sorry.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.040
(GASPS)

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.120
Oh my goodness! Nemo, are you okay?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.240
I said, "Not now." You've done enough.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.680
I have? Oh no. But I can fix it.
I can. I'll go get help.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.280
You know what you can do, Dory?
You can go wait over there.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.040
Go wait over there and forget.
It's what you do best.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.640
You're right. I don't know why I thought
I could do this.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.200
Find my family. I can't do this.
I'm so sorry. I'll fix it.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.120
-NEMO: I'm okay.
-Well, I'm gonna get help. Okay?

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.320
Okay? I can do that. I'll be--
It'll be all right, Nemo.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.800
Hello? Someone? Hello?

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.880
Anyone? Hello? Anyone?

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.480
SIGOURNEY ON SPEAKER: Hello.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.040
-Hello?
-I'm Sigourney Weaver.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.040
Oh. Hi, Sigourney. I need your help.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.160
Won't you please join us...

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.720
Oh. Great, great, great.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.120
As we explore the wonders
of the Pacific Ocean...

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.560
and the amazing life it holds within.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.880
Witness the majesty
of the Beluga Whale.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.520
Sigourney Weaver, where are you?

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.680
Dory! There you are!

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.520
Guys! I found help. Sigourney Weaver's
gonna tell us where we are.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.840
-Look out!
-(SCREAMS)

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.680
-Oh, look at this!
-No respect for ocean life.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.040
-Marlin! Nemo!
-NEMO: Dory!

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.240
No, no, no. Not again! Not again!

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.920
Let's take her inside
and see how she does.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.040
(DORY SCREAMS)

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.520
NEMO: Dory! Dory!

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.360
MARLIN: Don't worry, Dory! Stay calm.
We'll come find you!

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.040
SIGOURNEY: And welcome to
the Marine Life Institute...

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.400
where we believe in Rescue,
Rehabilitation and Release.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.200
DORY: Marlin? Nemo?

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.880
(DORY PANTING)

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.360
Hello? Hello? Can you help me?

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.360
Me help you? (SNEEZES)

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.040
Ugh. (SCREAMS)

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.040
Oh. (GASPS)

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.520
Huh? What's happening? Help?

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.840
MAN: Looks like we're done here.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.280
WOMAN: Dude, cut it out.
You're a scientist. We talked about this.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.760
MAN: Oh, come on. It's funny.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.400
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.640
DORY: Oh boy. Okay. This is--

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.040
I'll be fine, I just need to find
a way out and...

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.960
If I could just-- Get a hold of yourself,

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.080
-get a hold of yourself.
-(YELPS)

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.080
You'll be fine, everything's fine,
think positively.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.000
-Hey, you.
-Oh.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:30.960
Spinner.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.600
Oh, thank goodness. Hi, I'm Dory. I'm--

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.640
Name's Hank. How sick are you?

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.960
Sick? I'm sick?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.120
Why else would you be in quarantine?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.240
Oh no! How long do I have?
I have to find my family.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.000
All right. Now don't get hysterical--
Uh-oh. Not good.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.760
What? What is it? What happened?
(GASPS) What's that?

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.480
That there is bad news.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.000
It's a transport tag for fish
who can't cut it inside the institute.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.280
They get transferred to permanent digs.
An aquarium.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.040
In Cleveland.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.360
Fish in here, go back in the ocean.
Cleveland fish, stay there forever.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.080
(GASPS) Cleveland? No!
I can't go to the Cleveland.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.080
I have to get to the Jewel of Morro Bay,
California and find my family.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.080
That's this place.
The Marine Life Institute.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.000
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
You're here.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.280
You mean I'm from here?

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.800
(GASPS) My parents are here.
I have to get to them.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.200
So what exhibit are you from?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.320
Wait. I'm from an exhibit?
Which one? I have to get there.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.600
Hmm. That's a hard one, kid.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.960
Unless... Nah.
Never work. It's too crazy.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.120
What do you mean? Just tell me.
I'm okay with crazy.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.280
You know, I could see that?
Well, there's one thing I can think of...

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.360
to help you get to your family.
If I just take--

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.640
Yes! Great idea.
You take me to find them.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.800
Why didn't I think of that?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.840
Uh, no, no, no.
If I just take your tag...

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.680
I can take your place on the transport
truck then you can go back inside...

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.000
and find your family.
All you have to do is give me the tag.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.200
What tag?
(GASPS) There's a tag on my fin!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.800
How could you forget
you have a tag on your fin?

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:57.840
Oh no. I'm sorry. I--
I suffer from short-term memory loss.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.280
You don't remember
what we were talking about?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.080
Mm-mm. Not a clue.
What were we talking about?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.040
Um, you were about to give me your tag.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.320
Well, I kind of like my tag.
Why do you want it?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.360
So I can go to--

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.480
So I can go to Cleveland.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:13.760
Cleveland? Mmm.
I hear good things

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.000
about Cleveland.
Why do you want to go?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.320
Because if I stay here I'm gonna get
released back to the ocean.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.680
And I have extremely
unpleasant memories of that place.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.200
(EXHALES)

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.440
I just want to live in a glass box alone.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.200
That's all I want. So give me your tag!

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.720
Hey, man, don't touch my tag!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.040
(SIGHS)

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:31.680
Look...

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.960
(SLURPS)

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.080
I don't work here.
It's not like I have a map of this place.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.440
(GASPS) A map! Good idea.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.640
You take me to the map, I figure out
where my parents are. Oh boy.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:50.280
All right. If I get you to your family
will you give me--

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.040
I don't have much. Um, I--
How about if I give you this tag?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.720
Great idea.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.480
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.800
MARLIN: Are you absolutely
sure that's what I said?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.760
"Go wait over there and forget.
That's what you do best."

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:08.920
-Yeah, Dad.
-I said that?

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.880
You said that, Dory swam to the surface,

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.240
and she got taken by some--

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.560
All right, I don't want to hear
the whole story again.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.920
I was just asking about the one part
because, look, if I said that--

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.920
I'm not positive I did.
It's actually a compliment because...

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.120
I asked her to wait and I said,
"It's what you do best."

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.280
So I-- Oh, it's my fault!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.280
It's all my fault she got kidnapped
and taken into whatever this place is.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:33.080
What if it's a restaurant?

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.560
Oy! You two! Shut it!

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:39.600
Yeah, we're trying to sleep!
You interrupted my favorite dream!

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.440
Is that the one about you
laying on this rock?

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.960
-Yeah.
-Oh, that is a good one.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.800
-Oh yeah, isn't it? Yeah.
-It's one of my favorites.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:46.640
NEMO: Uh, excuse us. Hello!

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:47.480
-Son! Son.
-We're trying to--

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.800
Those are sea lions.
They are natural predators.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.000
They could pounce at any moment.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.480
(YAWNING)

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.760
Uh, they don't look very pouncy.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.480
That's what they want you to think.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.320
Just get behind me
and let me do the talking.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.880
Excuse me, we're worried
about our friend. Is that a restaurant?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.280
(LAUGHING)

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.800
Mate, it's not a restaurant.
Your friend is okay.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.120
-She is?
-It's a fish hospital.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.520
Sigourney Weaver says she'll be
rescued, rehabilitated, and released.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:17.680
She'll be in and out in a jiff.
We should know.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.440
-Nasal parasite.
-Anemia.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.200
All fixed up and sent on our way.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.400
Oh thank goodness.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.560
Sure, that's all right.
Don't you worry ab--

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.800
-BOTH: Gerald, get off the rock!
-Shove off, Gerald! Come on. Off! Off!

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:33.840
-Get off! Now you know better! Off!
-Off! Off! Off! Off!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.840
Don't you worry about a thing.
That place is the Marine Life Institute.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.120
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.120
(GASPS) She was right.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.360
It looks like Dory
can do something besides forget.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.320
Thank you, Nemo. Thank you for that.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.520
So how are we gonna get inside?

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.200
Wait. You want to get inside MLI?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.040
Desperately. Our friend is in there.
Lost, alone.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.360
She's scared.
She'll have no idea what to do.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.560
Oh, we know a way.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:00.880
You do?

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.400
BOTH: Ooo-roo.
Ooo-roo-roo. Ooo-roo.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.560
-What are they doing?
-I don't know. It sounds bad.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.520
DORY: Are we there yet?
HANK: Sh. Keep it down!

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.480
Hank, I'm so glad I found you.
It feels like-- I-- Destiny.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.520
For what must be the millionth time,
it's not destiny.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.920
Uh-oh. Have I said "destiny" before?
I'm sorry.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.200
I'm just so nervous
because I'm gonna meet my parents.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.560
I haven't seen them in I don't even know
how long because...

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.880
-you see I suffer from short-term--
-HANK: Short-term memory loss.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.680
Look, no more talking. Okay?
I don't like talking.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.240
I don't like chatter and questions.
And, "How are you? Oh I'm fine."

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.360
(PHONE RINGING)

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.560
"How are you? I'm fine too."
News flash -nobody's fine.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.520
Oh, I'm fine. How are you?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.680
(SIGHS)

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.760
-Hank, look, there's a map!
-Sh!

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.560
The plan is you're gonna read that
and figure out where your parents live.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.560
Then I'm on the truck to Cleveland.
You got it?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.920
Got it. What was the first part again?

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.360
Ugh.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.600
What? The octopus escaped again?

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.280
Wow. Look at all the exhibits.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.400
How can you do this park in one day?
Seriously.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:53.880
-Pick one!
-Okay. Um...

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.600
(GROANS) Well,
tell everyone to keep an eye out.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.400
We're supposed to be releasing
the octopus back to the ocean today.

